<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Edinburgh–Northampton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1328">1328</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Edinburgh-Northampton · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>–Northampton, agreed at Edinburgh in March 1328 and ratified by the English parliament at Northampton in May, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> recognised Robert I as king of an independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and gave up its claim to overlordship, and Robert's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> was to marry Edward III's sister Joan. Edward III later repudiated it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-edinburgh-northampton.jpg" alt="Treaty of Edinburgh–Northampton" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Graeme Smith · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holyrood_Abbey_-_geograph.org.uk_-_568988.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
